    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the project, and it passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change assigns `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nI implemented it as a **pure derived value in the MapStruct mapper**, mirroring the existing `householdId`/`displayName`/`initials` pattern rather than storing new state or adding a pipeline step. This keeps structural impact minimal \u2014 no changes to the large `Owner` entity, no new function class, no YAML wiring, and every touched method stays trivially simple.\n\nThree files touched:\n- **`mapper/MembershipNumber.java`** (new) \u2014 a small cohesive helper: `of(customerCode, registrationDate)` returns `customerCode + \"-M\" + last-two-digits-of-year`, computed with `registrationDate.getYear() % 100` and `%02d` zero-padding.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to the helper (the method body stays generated/simple).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nBecause it's derived from the owner's own persisted fields, it works identically on the create response and on subsequent fetches, and is seed-independent. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
